# Site configuration for the PegasusAI Studio OOD app.
# Install as /etc/ood/config/apps/pegasus-studio/site.env on the PORTAL host.
# template/script.sh.erb bakes it into each session's job script at render
# time, so compute nodes need no copy. Values are shell; $HOME expands on the
# session host to the user's REAL home.

# --- The image ---
# Built from ood-app/studio-el9.def. Must be readable on every session host.
STUDIO_SIF=/opt/pegasus-ai/studio/studio-el9.sif

# --- Where Studio lives (#482) ---
# Studio runs with this directory as its $HOME, so it never writes into the
# user's real home. A user can override it per session in the form. It must
# be on storage the HTCondor submit host also mounts at the same path:
# DAGMan and remote planning read the workflow's submit directory from there.
#STUDIO_HOME_DEFAULT=$HOME/pegasus-studio

# Entries of the real home linked into the Studio home when present (and not
# already there). The default keeps HTCondor submission and git identity
# working. Add .ssh for SSH-based submission or git over ssh. Set it to an
# empty string to link nothing.
#STUDIO_HOME_INHERIT=".condor/tokens.d .gitconfig"

# Extra arguments for `apptainer run`: scratch or project binds, --nv.
#STUDIO_APPTAINER_ARGS="--bind /scratch --bind /project"

# --- HTCondor ---
# If the session host is itself an access point, nothing to set.
# Otherwise point the client at the remote one. Users additionally need an
# IDTOKEN in ~/.condor/tokens.d (linked in by STUDIO_HOME_INHERIT above).
#
# SCHEDD_HOST is what makes this work at all: pegasus-run calls plain
# `condor_submit`, which otherwise looks for a *local* schedd and fails with
# "Can't find address of local schedd" on any node that isn't the AP.
# Use the FULLY QUALIFIED name; a short name fails with the same message.
#_CONDOR_COLLECTOR_HOST=cm.lab.example.org
#_CONDOR_SCHEDD_HOST=ap.lab.example.org

# --- Pegasus site catalog ---
# A published catalog from github.com/pegasushub/pegasus-site-catalogs for
# every user of this install. Unset: Studio's own pool (site "compute").
#STUDIO_SITE_CATALOG=unity.yml

# --- LLM access for the AI assistant ---
# Leave unset and users add their own provider and key in Settings, or point
# at a gateway the lab runs.
#STUDIO_LLM_GATEWAY_URL=https://llm.lab.example.org/v1

# The hosted Pegasus agent endpoint used by pegasus-analyzer.
#STUDIO_PEGASUS_AGENT_URL=https://api.pegasus-ai.org
